Table locations [headercolor: #0EA5E9] {
    Note: '''
A physical site that holds stock: an outlet (store) or a warehouse. kind selects the
site role; kind-specific rules stay in the application.
'''

    id           BIGINT      [pk, increment]
    kind         TEXT        [not null, note: 'store or warehouse.']
    name         TEXT        [not null]
    description  TEXT        [not null, default: '']
    location_lat DOUBLE      [note: 'WGS84 latitude; NULL when unknown.']
    location_lng DOUBLE      [note: 'WGS84 longitude; NULL when unknown.']
    is_active    BOOLEAN     [not null, default: true]
    created_at   timestamptz [not null, default: `NOW()`]
    updated_at   timestamptz
    created_by   BIGINT
    updated_by   BIGINT

    Indexes {
        name [unique, name: 'uq_locations_name']
    }
}

Table inventories [headercolor: #16A34A] {
    Note: '''
Current stock of one SKU at one location. The pair is unique; stock is the running
balance, with movements and audits recorded separately.

inventories cascades from both parents: a deleted product, SKU, or regenerated catalog
removes the affected stock rows, and deleting a location removes its stock. The
database does not protect stock: the application must guard these operations, warn the
user with the affected SKUs and the locations and quantities on hand, and record a
write-off in stock_movements when destroying stock.
'''

    id          BIGINT      [pk, increment]
    location_id BIGINT      [not null]
    sku_id      BIGINT      [not null]
    stock       BIGINT      [not null, default: 0]
    created_at  timestamptz [not null, default: `NOW()`]
    updated_at  timestamptz
    created_by  BIGINT
    updated_by  BIGINT

    Indexes {
        (location_id, sku_id) [unique, name: 'uq_inventories_location_id_sku_id']
        sku_id                [name: 'idx_inventories_sku_id']
    }
}

Table stock_movements [headercolor: #15803D] {
    Note: '''
Append-only record of stock moving in, out, or between locations. Rows are never
updated or deleted, so this is the audit trail behind inventories.stock.

quantity is a positive magnitude; direction comes from the locations. A receipt has
src_location_id NULL, an issue (sale, write-off) has dest_location_id NULL, and a
transfer sets both. reason classifies the movement (receipt, sale, transfer,
adjustment, write_off, return); the application validates the value set because there
are no CHECK constraints.

Each reference carries a name snapshot captured when the movement is written:
sku_label, src_location_name, and dest_location_name. References are nullable and
ON DELETE SET NULL, so deleting a SKU, product, or location never erases the movement,
and the snapshot keeps it readable. The application must fill the snapshots at write
time; they cannot be recovered later.
'''

    id                 BIGINT      [pk, increment]
    sku_id             BIGINT      [note: 'NULL once the SKU or its product is deleted; sku_label keeps the snapshot.']
    sku_label          TEXT        [note: 'SKU label at the time of the movement; NULL when unknown.']
    src_location_id    BIGINT      [note: 'Origin location; NULL for stock entering the system.']
    src_location_name  TEXT        [note: 'Origin location name at the time of the movement; NULL when there is no source.']
    dest_location_id   BIGINT      [note: 'Destination location; NULL for stock leaving the system.']
    dest_location_name TEXT        [note: 'Destination location name at the time of the movement; NULL when there is no destination.']
    quantity           BIGINT      [not null, note: 'Positive magnitude; direction comes from the locations.']
    reason             TEXT        [not null, note: 'receipt, sale, transfer, adjustment, write_off, or return.']
    created_at         timestamptz [not null, default: `NOW()`]

    Indexes {
        sku_id             [name: 'idx_stock_movements_sku_id']
        src_location_id    [name: 'idx_stock_movements_src_location_id']
        dest_location_id   [name: 'idx_stock_movements_dest_location_id']
        created_at         [name: 'idx_stock_movements_created_at']
    }
}
